\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Compatible choices at successive depths}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{Every hierarchical precision preserves the class-constant fields
and their perpendicular fluctuations. The rescaled class mean in
\ref{fdip-00C1} therefore removes the finest coefficient and shifts
the others. The fixed-ratio family of \ref{fdip-00C2} repeats this
operation at every depth. How much freedom remains if compatibility
is required but the fixed-ratio formula is not prescribed?}
